I like the idea! Here's an idea I gave some thought a while back. It'd
require major changes to code, but I think it would be pretty neat :

A Pet class : The idea is that you are the pet to a normal character
class (picked at random) and you have to help them get through the game.
The problem would be that the present 'AI' code for the pets would not
be sufficient to keep a character alive. (Anyone written an auto-nethack
player out there? Now there's a challenge for the budding perl programmers
amongst you!) Perhaps a pet would have the ability to change its owner,
and of course it could rob shops with complete impunity. Also, since
polymorph wouldn't wear off, if it could convince its owner to zap
polymorph at it, or it found a polymorph trap...!

I suspect this is just a curiosity, since I don't have time to code it,
and it'd be quite a big job, but I think it would be fun. If I ever get
a free month, then I might just give it a go... What do you think, folks?

